  "verseCount": 34,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "15",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "1KI 15"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "15",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Abijah King of Judah",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the eighteenth year of the reign of Jeroboam son of Nebat, Abijah",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "became king of Judah,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and he reigned in Jerusalem three years. His mother's name was Maakah daughter of Abishalom.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He committed all the sins his father had done before him; his heart was not fully devoted to the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.3",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.3"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "his God, as the heart of David his forefather had been.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, for David's sake the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.4",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.4"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "his God gave him a lamp in Jerusalem by raising up a son to succeed him and by making Jerusalem strong.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For David had done what was right in the eyes of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.5",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.5"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and had not failed to keep any of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.5",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.5"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s commands all the days of his life—except in the case of Uriah the Hittite.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There was war between Abijah",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "and Jeroboam throughout Abijah's lifetime.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As for the other events of Abijah's reign, and all he did, are they not written in the book of the annals of the kings of Judah? There was war between Abijah and Jeroboam.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Abijah rested with his ancestors and was buried in the City of David. And Asa his son succeeded him as king.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Asa King of Judah",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the twentieth year of Jeroboam king of Israel, Asa became king of Judah,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and he reigned in Jerusalem forty-one years. His grandmother's name was Maakah daughter of Abishalom.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Asa did what was right in the eyes of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.11",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.11"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ", as his father David had done.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He expelled the male shrine prostitutes from the land and got rid of all the idols his ancestors had made.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He even deposed his grandmother Maakah from her position as queen mother, because she had made a repulsive image for the worship of Asherah. Asa cut it down and burned it in the Kidron Valley.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Although he did not remove the high places, Asa's heart was fully committed to the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.14",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.14"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "all his life.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He brought into the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.15",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.15"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "the silver and gold and the articles that he and his father had dedicated.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel throughout their reigns.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah and fortified Ramah to prevent anyone from leaving or entering the territory of Asa king of Judah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Asa then took all the silver and gold that was left in the treasuries of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.18",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.18"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "'s temple and of his own palace. He entrusted it to his officials and sent them to Ben-Hadad son of Tabrimmon, the son of Hezion, the king of Aram, who was ruling in Damascus.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Let there be a treaty between me and you,\" he said, \"as there was between my father and your father. See, I am sending you a gift of silver and gold. Now break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel so he will withdraw from me.\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ben-Hadad agreed with King Asa and sent the commanders of his forces against the towns of Israel. He conquered Ijon, Dan, Abel Beth Maakah and all Kinnereth in addition to Naphtali.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When Baasha heard this, he stopped building Ramah and withdrew to Tirzah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then King Asa issued an order to all Judah—no one was exempt—and they carried away from Ramah the stones and timber Baasha had been using there. With them King Asa built up Geba in Benjamin, and also Mizpah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.22"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As for all the other events of Asa's reign, all his achievements, all he did and the cities he built, are they not written in the book of the annals of the kings of Judah? In his old age, however, his feet became diseased.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Asa rested with his ancestors and was buried with them in the city of his father David. And Jehoshaphat his son succeeded him as king.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.24"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Nadab King of Israel",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nadab son of Jeroboam became king of Israel in the second year of Asa king of Judah, and he reigned over Israel two years.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He did evil in the eyes of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.26",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.26"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ", following the ways of his father and committing the same sin his father had caused Israel to commit.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.26"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Baasha son of Ahijah from the tribe of Issachar plotted against him, and he struck him down at Gibbethon, a Philistine town, while Nadab and all Israel were besieging it.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Baasha killed Nadab in the third year of Asa king of Judah and succeeded him as king.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.28"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As soon as he began to reign, he killed Jeroboam's whole family. He did not leave Jeroboam anyone that breathed, but destroyed them all, according to the word of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.29",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.29"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "given through his servant Ahijah the Shilonite.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "This happened because of the sins Jeroboam had committed and had caused Israel to commit, and because he aroused the anger of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "1KI.15.30",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "1KI.15.30"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of Israel.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.30"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As for the other events of Nadab's reign, and all he did, are they not written in the book of the annals of the kings of Israel?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1KI 15:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel throughout their reigns.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1KI.15.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1KI.15.32"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Baasha King of Israel",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
